# The reference puts the first check of an object whose check period is
# closed at a moment of its own choosing after the period opens. For this
# service that was second 142, after the end of the run: the next check in
# the state it saved.
first a-soon@142000 the reference had planned its first check for after the end of the run

# The host c and its service are first checked in the same millisecond.
# Whose result is read first decides whether the service goes through a
# soft state. In real time that is not the same from run to run.
ignore-real c the order of two results a millisecond apart
ignore-real c-onc the order of two results a millisecond apart
ignore-log-real c the order of two results a millisecond apart
ignore-log-real c;onc the order of two results a millisecond apart
